+Maphuma+%26+Shoday+Nakupenda+-+I+Love+You+%28Vigro+Deep+Remix%29+%5Bfeat.+Davido%2C+Zlatan+%26+Al+Xapo%5D&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["2026 2026 LVRN Records (Love Renaissance), under exclusive license from TXC Enterprises (PTY) LTD."]}, {"t": 3360, "time": "00:56:00", "artist": "Xduppy & Angekebabuye mc", "title": "Lwetse (feat. DJ Maphorisa & Mluusician)", "conf": "mid", "links": [{"label": "bandcamp", "url": "https://bandcamp.com/search?q=Xduppy+%26+Angekebabuye+mc+Lwetse+%28feat.+DJ+Maphorisa+%26+Mluusician%29", "search": true}, {"label": "youtube", "url": "https://www.youtube.com/results?search_query=Xduppy+%26+Angekebabuye+mc+Lwetse+%28feat.+DJ+Maphorisa+%26+Mluusician%29", "search": true}, {"label": "soundcloud", "url": "https://soundcloud.com/search?q=Xduppy+%26+Angekebabuye+mc+Lwetse+%28feat.+DJ+Maphorisa+%26+Mluusician%29", "search": true}, {"label": "spotify", "url": "https://open.spotify.com/search/Xduppy+%26+Angekebabuye+mc+Lwetse+%28feat.+DJ+Maphorisa+%26+Mluusician%29", "search": true}, {"label": "apple", "url": "https://music.apple.com/au/song/1886738960", "search": false}, {"label": "deezer", "url": "https://www.deezer.com/search/Xduppy+%26+Angekebabuye+mc+Lwetse+%28feat.+DJ+Maphorisa+%26+Mluusician%29", "search": true}, {"label": "discogs", "url": "https://www.discogs.com/search/?q=Xduppy+%26+Angekebabuye+mc+Lwetse+%28feat.+DJ+Maphorisa+%26+Mluusician%29&type=all", "search": true}], "notes": ["2026 New Money Gang Records"]}], "counts": {"high": 0, "mid": 12, "low": 8}, "transcripts": [{"start": "00:16:16", "end": "00:17:36", "text": "You're tuned in to The Yanos Show on FBi Radio 94.5 with myself DJ TeeSoul and I hope you're all having an amazing Saturday. I don't know what mood I'm in as per usual. I'm feeling very, I don't even know if I have the right word for it. I'm in a bit of everything today. I came in pretty hardcore and now I'm feeling very, very housey, very chill and we'll see where we end up by the end of the hour but with that being said there is a lot to catch everybody up on on the last couple weeks in the space in the scene and kind of what's been going on in terms of DJing artists kind of yeah everything that's been happening if you've missed out on anything there are still a couple more events coming up in the next few weeks that I'll definitely put a bit of a spotlight on so there definitely is a chance for everyone to get involved but we do have the whole hour together let me know what you've been listening to if there's anything you want to hear in particular and you know how it goes on this show we kind of find out where we want to go by the end of it but it's always a good time anyway but with that being said stay tuned this is the honor show"}, {"start": "00:42:54", "end": "00:47:35", "text": "You are tuning in to The Unoff Show on FBi Radio 94.5 and somehow we're left with T-minus 20 minutes left on this week's show. But I did again get caught up in all of it. I played a couple of throwbacks I want to say. i feel like i was mid 2024 2023 in some of that set which was such a good feeling because i feel like so many of the great music that came out at the peak of sort of when piano was really being pushed was when a lot of that music was coming out and again to be able to share it is such a privilege i think there's so much music that gets sort of put out into this space and it is very saturated as is any genre of music but yeah just being able to kind of go back and see how far it's come is just so it's so interesting to see what the evolution has been like over the last couple years and how alive the genre kind of is and on the topic of that actually I saw a video today and there was a guy talking about what artists do we all think survived the evolution of Amapiano so his main focus was on vocalistic and if anyone knows vocalistic he's probably one of the biggest if not the biggest vocalist in Amapiano that we have he is pretty what's the word fluid fluid that's the word I'm looking for with his own sound he knows how to get onto the right sound he knows who to work with and I guess it's all a business move in his from his side of things but as an artist he is able to just ride each wave as they come because with this genre there's so many different trends so many different artists that come and go and he's probably been one of the ones that have stayed stayed up the entire time which is really hard to do in six years I think that's probably been the peak of piano the last six years I would say and for him to still basically be at the top of vocalists is insane and I wanted to ask and see what everyone else thought if there's anyone else that comes to mind and if you do think of anyone send me a text on 0435 123 945 and I also wanted to talk about the last couple of weeks again last saturday so a week ago now we had the privilege of having dub and gogo in australia she was played in sydney last saturday night and personally she is one of my inspirations if not my biggest as a dj especially as a woman in this space she has been someone i've always kind of looked to for again that inspiration where can i go with this what can I do with this and to have her just like in the flesh was insane a lovely woman a great personality just someone who loves the game someone who loves to see other people win someone who is so willing to push other people as well to do bigger things so it was amazing to even meet her to open up for her that was amazing anyone who was there could probably say the same thing but in two weeks on the 25th of september we've got two bunnies coming on tour to australia alongside or headlining with sars actually another really big acrobeats artist but two bunnies are some great producers they have made some of the biggest tracks the biggest viral tracks also of the last couple of years in the scene and i'll be playing there a couple of my other phase will be playing there it's a pretty stacked lineup a very evenly spread lineup i love when a lineup is good you know it just suits everyone the lineup makes sense and i think sounds of afro beats did a really good thing with their lineup and for anyone who's free that night the 25th i think that's a friday night please come down it's at bella that's in bella vista actually so out west so there's really no excuses but there should be a couple more things happening after then but that'll be a problem for the next time that I speak to you all but if you don't hear from me again thank you for tuning in we've got a couple more tracks to round out this week's show again if you have anything to tell me send me a text on 0435 123 945 this is the honor show"}], "fbi_json": [{"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:00:00"}, "track": {"title": "Pop Culture", "artists": [{"name": "Madeon"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "low"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:01:00"}, "track": {"title": "SG 09.2", "artists": [{"name": "CarLo M. Lesuper"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "low"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:02:00"}, "track": {"title": "This Is My House", "artists": [{"name": "DJ K-SEXY"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "low"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:03:00"}, "track": {"title": "Mind, Body, Soul (feat. Tkcreedlion)", "artists": [{"name": "Jussgigi & Tshimza Stellies"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "low"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:04:00"}, "track": {"title": "This Dance (feat. Kabza De Small & MDU aka TRP)", "artists": [{"name": "Tycoon"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "mid"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:07:00"}, "track": {"title": "Reset Time", "artists": [{"name": "Mpekzin DaSoul"}]}, "isPremiere": false, "_confidence": "low"}, {"timestamp": {"enabled": true, "formatted": "00:08:00"}, "track": {"title": "Thriller (feat. Kabza De Small)", "artists": [{"name": "Shakes & Les & Tycoon"}]}, "isPremier